    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0289" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.82/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-08">January 8,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I presented Mr. Baker’s request to the Commissioners at the meeting this morning,
                    and Mr. Baker also spoke to them before their meeting with the newspaper
                    correspondents.</p>
                <p>It did not seem practical to have the newspaper correspondents attend the initial
                    meeting of the Allied Delegates, if that is what was meant by Mr. Baker’s
                    request. It is thought probable that provision would be made for the newspaper
                    correspondents to be present at the first formal meeting of the Conference.</p>
                <p>Mr. Baker has already been advised of the Commissioners’ views in this
                    matter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leland Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
